WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.112
We will begin with the Vector reduction
test item from

00:00:03.112 --> 00:00:06.050
the guide. It checks that summing the
integers from

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:09.220
one to ten thousand gives fifty million,
five thousand.

00:00:09.351 --> 00:00:13.032
The runner needs TestItemRunner version
one point three point

00:00:13.032 --> 00:00:16.472
two or newer, along with TestItems and the
package's test

00:00:16.472 --> 00:00:20.576
dependencies. Discover the items in the
Testing view and select one.

00:00:20.707 --> 00:00:24.771
Tags can narrow the performance selection,
and explicit repetitions

00:00:24.771 --> 00:00:28.957
control how many fresh processes are
requested. There is no automatic

00:00:28.957 --> 00:00:32.717
warmup of a native test item. Read the
item before running it.

00:00:32.849 --> 00:00:35.599
Its setup, operations and correctness
assertion

00:00:35.599 --> 00:00:37.939
define the scope that is being observed.

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:41.651
If an item builds data, performs file
access or includes

00:00:41.651 --> 00:00:45.358
several operations, do not describe its
result as the cost

00:00:45.358 --> 00:00:48.938
of one isolated function without checking
that boundary.
